## 0 · The headline numbers

- **FACT.** There were 311 commits in 11 days, 0 tags, and `l2=2` of 20 flows across 46 landings (SA:12, SA:38, SA:46).
- **FACT.** 105 gate/cold-clone runs took 38.6 machine-hours. 19 of the 105 (18%) measured nothing, and the gate caught 0 confirmed product defects (SA:57, CA:74).
- **FACT.** "Nearly every real defect came from independent review, planted faults and mutation" (SA:59). Plants were 842/868 killed, and every survivor was a real gap (NWOW:19).
- **FACT.** The last ship, deep-diff-forge, reached v0.1.0 11 h 53 m after its first commit. It had one prose spec, one layer per commit, no design rounds, and reviews after shipping. Its process files were 0.11× the product (SA:29-35).
- **FACT.** `l2` first moved 2 → 3 at `dfb32d5` on 2026-09-30, two days after the flow ratchet and the host-record L2 kind were adopted (LR-dfb32d5:13, DR:1737-1750).
- **FACT** *(measured now)*. `just friction` gives `verdict=MEASURED retry_rate=0.0184 commands=217` on the latest transcript (seed baseline 0.041 on 2026-09-04; 0.0158 on 2026-09-28, AH:233). This is friction that was paid, not friction that was avoided (PR:587-589).

## 1 · Inefficient loops

| # | Loop | Evidence (path:line, numbers) | Cost | Root cause (structural) | v4 mechanism | Control that proves it | Tag |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| L1 | **Per-landing serial confirmation.** Every slice paid a repo gate, a cold clone and a publication with its own cold clone. | NWOW:17 "≈ 80 min per landing, ≈ ⅔ of landing latency"; NWOW:18 "≈ 0" defects found by gate, cold clone and publication in the window. Gate ≈1,589–1,836 s and cold ≈1,579–1,807 s at every landing (LR-7ed3728:12-13, LR-0c3757a:9-10, LR-0b4637e:10-11). | 38.6 machine-h over 105 runs (SA:57) | Confirmation was coupled to every commit instead of to the ship (C3 upheld 2/2, SA:48) | **Tier map in the scaffold:** `gate.toml` declares each step's tier (commit / stack / cut), and the landing tool refuses to run a Tier-2 step on a single-slice range. The cold clone runs once per stack tip, never per slice. | Plant a 1-commit range and require `tier2 refused: range=1 slice`. The landing record prints `gate_minutes_per_l2_delta=`. | FACT (cost), INTERP (mechanism) |
| L2 | **A record-only commit pays a full gate and cold clone.** | `dfb32d5` added one JSON record plus a `.gitignore` line, and still ran gate 84/84 then cold 84/84 (LR-dfb32d5:3-7); the gate-run stamps are 02:57 and 03:27. | ≈60 min wall for 2 files | The gate has no notion of which steps a diff can affect | **Diff-scoped step selection:** each step declares its `subject_globs`, and a diff touching none of them skips the step with a printed `skipped=<step> reason=subject_untouched`. The whole gate still runs at a cut. | A control diff touching only `evidence/` must print `ran=` equal to the steps whose globs match, and one touching `src/` must run all of them. | FACT (commit), INTERP (≈60 min from the stamps) |
| L3 | **Hand-bumped count literals.** Every test addition edits gate literals. | 74 of 86 src commits hand-edit t25 census literals, 3,646 lines churned (NWOW:21). 89/119 (75%) edit `check-quality`/t25, and 87 of those change a count literal (SA:48). 141/205 (CA:72). The t25 pin lives in two literals (MEM/hee3-gate-t25-count-pin:15-17), and there was a third home of the t04 count (`B14-store-runtime-20260926/DESIGN.md:3308`). | 3,646 lines churned; serial collisions on one file | The gate stores expectations as authored numbers: a second door on what cargo already knows | **Derived gate from day 0:** expectations are relations (tests that ran ⊇ base `--list` minus `Removes-test:` trailers; every manifest target runs ≥ 1 test), with no count literal anywhere (SA:78-80, DR:1547-1551). | `retired=N/M` census over all tools; a planted emptied test file must not lower the expectation; `grep -E 'Ran [0-9]+ tests'` over tools returns 0. | FACT |
| L4 | **First gate on a fresh worktree fails on an input the worktree lacks.** | A fresh worktree lacks `tools/rust-offline-inputs/` and `tools/sqlite-inputs/`, and 13 quality tests error at `copytree` (`T00-session-20260924/completion-map/WAVE1-INTEGRATION.md:67-69`). `serde-1.0.229.crate` was absent and a clean `--no-local` clone failed identically (`T28/B14c-one-composer-20260927/S1/NOTES.md:123`). Undeclared fixture inputs failed the gate at clippy after 25 min, three times (MEM/hee3-gate-declared-inputs:11-22). | ≈25 min per recurrence ×3, plus manual copies | Fetched inputs are git-ignored side files; the gate's world is a hand-kept path list | **`provision` verb plus an input manifest:** one command materialises every fetched input from a content-addressed store, and the gate's first step refuses by name (`missing_input=<path> sha=`) before any build. Test fixtures are declared by directory (`tree_files`), never by member. | A control deletes one bundle crate and requires the step-0 refusal naming it in < 5 s. `include_census` stays (MEM/hee3-gate-declared-inputs:24-28). | FACT |
| L5 | **The first gate fails on process hygiene invisible to dev runs.** | A `sleep 30 &` stand-in → `descendants_detected` 25 min late (MEM/gate-detects-leaked-descendants:11-21). bwrap's pid 1 was orphaned to the subreaper (LR-0c3757a:30-32). git 2.55's detached maintenance left zombies at `fd0f11f` (LR-b5367bc:20-26). | ≥ 3 gate+cold reruns (≈60 min each) | The dev runner and the gate runner differ: only the gate is a subreaper | **One runner:** `cargo test` in dev, the precount and the gate all go through the same `run_bounded` subreaper wrapper (scaffold `tools/run`). Dev runs report `descendants=` too. Temp repos get `-c maintenance.auto=false` by default. | Plant a test that forks `sleep`, and require the **dev** run to print `descendants_detected=true`. | FACT |
| L6 | **The precount cannot discriminate.** Its rc is red on every healthy tree. | `precount rc=101` on `b5367bc`, identical to N6b's; the reds are env-bound tests (t13 17, t21 22, t21 analysis 1) (LR-b5367bc:29-33, LR-7ed3728:22-24). rustdoc is not in the precount, so `be71bfb` failed the gate on `default-rustdoc` (LR-0b4637e:18). | ≈60 min rerun (INTERP); a check that is red everywhere is scenery | Env-bound tests have no declared environment; the precount is a reconstruction of the gate (two doors) | **Precount = the gate's own Tier-1 subset**, generated from `gate.toml`, not a separate script. Env-bound tests declare `#[env_requires(...)]` and are reported as `skipped_env=N` by name, never as failures. | A healthy tree must give precount `rc=0 skipped_env=<named>`; a planted rustdoc broken link must red the precount. | FACT |
| L7 | **Timing margins consumed by load.** | t21 has a 12 s margin on 180 s, and a load-induced timeout costs a 50-minute rerun (MEM/no-builds-beside-a-gate:11-19). `default-release-tests-main` takes 149–155 s of 180 s (LR-0c3757a:34). S17b: 3 Deadline tests plus 6 noise tests fail under `-j 2` (DR:1812-1817). `t28_runtime.rs:1032` took 1.000605 s against a 1 s budget (MEM/no-builds-beside-a-gate:27). | 50 min per false red | Wall-clock budgets in tests plus a shared machine with no admission control | **Gate slot admission plus a printed margin:** each step records `elapsed/budget`, and the landing record lists steps above 80% of budget. Tests use logical clocks (F95 seam) instead of wall time, except for named hang-guards. `hee3-gate` flock slots (NWOW:88) become scaffold. | The landing record prints `margin_min=<step> <pct>`; a planted `sleep` in a test at 85% must appear in it. | FACT |
| L8 | **Edits under a running gate or battery void the run.** | 11 of 64 gate runs (17%) measured nothing (NWOW:22); 2 of those 11 were voided by edits (NWOW:88). Each voided run lost ≈25 min, twice in one session (MEM/never-edit-a-gated-worktree:11). A `git add` mid-battery committed a mutant (`181bc35`, MEM/never-stage-during-a-plant-battery:11-14). | ≈25 min ×2, plus a defective commit | The worktree is mutable while a verdict is being taken about it | **Gate on a snapshot, never on the live worktree:** the gate runs on `git archive <sha>` or a `--detach` worktree it owns. The live worktree is never the subject. Plant batteries run in their own copy. | Edit the live worktree mid-gate; the gate verdict must be unchanged and name `tree=<sha>`. | FACT |
| L9 | **Publication and corpus generation on the landing chain.** | 18–44 min per run; 4 of 20 runs failed on the corpus agreeing with itself; 92.3% of inserted lines are hash bookkeeping (DR:1580). 4 of 10 attempts failed on self-inflicted metadata, ≈2 h (NWOW:20). Landing→publication lag reached 94 and 98 min on 09-27 (`T00-stall-assessment-20260928/hee3-roi.md:65`). There were 25 `Publication for` commits since 09-23, then 11/week (AH:239). Graph, atlas and snapshot data came to `freed_bytes=296423514112` (DR:1629). | ≈2 h failures + 18–44 min × every landing + 296 GB | State was authored as prose and re-sealed by a publisher, then projected into the product (JU:32-49) | **No publisher.** Intent is small rows in the repo, every row names its reader ("no reader, no row"), state is computed on read, and a version cut is a tag carrying `flows= l2= evidenced=` (DR:1584-1600). | `grep -r 'Publication for'` in the v4 log = 0; every intent row resolves a reader (control: an orphan row reds). | FACT |
| L10 | **The corpus leaked into product semantics.** | The store's migration identity requires the corpus marker `-- HEE3-ANCHORS-END` (JU:66). 58,762 anchor lines across 79 tracked files, 2,403 of them in `Cargo.toml` (JU:44). 30 `src`/`tests` files falsely say "Engine coding is not authorized" (JU:45). Code-writing subagents made 4 corpus reads against 952 code reads (JU:39). | Unremovable coupling; a false message in the one channel agents read | Generated navigation was written into source files | **Source files carry no generated blocks.** A scaffold lint refuses `BEGIN…END` generated spans in `src/`, `tests/`, `migrations/` and manifests. Schema identity is a digest of the SQL itself. | A planted anchor block in `src/` reds the lint with the path. | FACT |
| L11 | **Diary and record writes break a pinned corpus.** | The publisher refused after diary appends, three times (MEM/diary-write-needs-recapture:13-15). A reviewer of the recapture stalled 2 h 40 min (MEM/recapture-review-needs-a-command-budget:11-18). Wrong-file appends went to a corpus output (MM:1473-1476). The pin is stale again today (DR:1902-1903). | ≈2.5 h per publication wait | Reflection corpora were captured as pinned inputs of the product corpus | **Evidence never pins the diary.** v4 intent rows may cite a diary entry by id, never by sha of a mutable file. | A diary append must leave every v4 check green (control: append a line, run the gate). | FACT |
| L12 | **Design-review round inflation in prose.** | B14a-2 had 4 rounds, all FAIL, with HIGH counts 5 → 4 → 3 (NWOW:23). R14–R23 each took exactly 2 rounds and none passed round 1. R23 alone cost 4 agents, 659,219 tokens and 187 tool calls (CA:88-91). B14's DESIGN.md is 4,412 lines / 444,728 B for one route item, against 6,502 lines for the whole forge spec (CA:85). | 659k tokens per round; ≈20 sub-slices for one route item (CA:92) | Interfaces were designed in prose, and reviewers found by reading what a compiler states in seconds (NWOW:28-31) | **Skeleton-first as a scaffold state machine:** `slice new` creates `FLOW.md` (≤ 1 page) and a compiling skeleton branch. The review tool refuses a design review whose subject sha does not compile (`cargo check`), and refuses a round 3. | The review tool on a prose-only range → `refused: no compiled skeleton`; round 3 → `refused: round cap 2; land buildable cut`. | FACT |
| L13 | **Detector rounds with a receding horizon.** | Rounds went 21 mutants all killed → 85 with 26 surviving → 63 → 127 with 36 surviving (CM:123-127, F128). A 42-control census still had 5 compiling false passes (MEM/census-receding-horizon:8-15). B14c-E cost 2,319 lines and two designs on a rule one symbol check settles (SA:61, DR:1486-1491). | ≈5.4 h wall (CA:77, INTERP) | A regex or lexer over a language the compiler parses; no budget on detectors | **Detector budget as an admission field:** every new check file needs a header of `trigger=<number> budget=1 round/1 session reader=`, and the `new-artifact` reflex blocks (not warns) in the v4 repo without it. Prefer compiler-decided rules (privacy, types, symbols). | The CI lint refuses a `tools/check-*` without the header; the survivors-per-round figure is printed. | FACT |
| L14 | **Plants that planted nothing or were killed for the wrong reason.** | Every t04 killer read NOT_COMPILED because the battery named a non-existent test target (`T28/B14-store-runtime-20260926/DESIGN.md:3313-3314`, MM:1688-1691). "A plant that fails to compile is not a kill" (`~/handoffs/HEE3_RESTART_20260923_LATE.md:94-95`). A plant killed by the lint law is a kill for the wrong reason (CM:174). A restore kept the mtime, so cargo ran the stale mutant and gave 3 spurious FAILs (MEM/plant-restore-mtime-trap:8-12). Plants hung past 300 s (`DESIGN.md:3673`). | One battery wasted per incident (UNMEASURED minutes) | Batteries were hand-written per slice (`plants-<slice>.py`), and each re-derived the primitives | **One battery harness in the scaffold:** it resolves killers against `cargo test -- --list` before planting (an unknown killer refuses), plants under `--cap-lints=warn`, restores with a fresh mtime and then `cargo clean -p`, writes a pid file, freezes the index, and counts `NOT_COMPILED`/`HUNG` as survivors. | The harness control plants an unknown killer name (must refuse), a lint-only plant (must be `not_a_kill`), and an mtime-preserving restore (must be detected). | FACT |
| L15 | **Mutation runs voided or owed.** | A shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` linked the unmutated lib: a hand plant failed 21 of 57 cases the tool said survived (MEM/mutation-target-dir-trap:14-15). A sweep landed as "owed" then found 21 survivors (MM:1329-1336). `store-doors` tested 0 mutants with `rc=4` twice (FIN:25). RA2: 178 listed, 21 survivors (DR:1809). | A whole run void; 21 survivors on main for ≈1 h | Two rules on one variable in opposite directions; mutation was not a landing step | **The mutation runner owns its target dir** (unsets `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` inside itself) and runs a one-compile precheck plant that must go red. It is a Tier-2 step scoped to changed store/policy files, and "owed" is not a landing state. | Precheck: a known plant must print `precheck=red`, else `verdict=VOID`. The landing tool refuses `mutation=owed`. | FACT |
| L16 | **Two doors on one rule, recurring.** | A scratchpad gate passed and the repo's own gate refused nine times (MM:1600-1610). A receipt caption contradicted the computed line (MM:765-772). A check contradicted an architecture decision twice in one wave (MM:895-930). The publication preflight had to be the publisher's own (NWOW:87). The t25 count lived in two or three places (L3). | Nine refusals; three documents saying "closed" for 2 h (MM:803-805) | Rules re-implemented beside their owner | **One door per rule, enumerated:** `rules.toml` maps each rule id → exactly one enforcing site. A census parses the check sources (`ast`/`syn`) and refuses a rule id enforced at two sites. | A planted duplicate enforcement site reds the census with both paths. | FACT |
| L17 | **Handover and state sprawl; wrong-file appends.** | 14 restart/handover notes, 281 KB, in 8 days (SA:52, C9 contested). *(Measured now)* 21 `HEE3_*` files, 714,986 B, in `~/handoffs` (6 HANDOVER, 11 RESTART). Updates were appended to a superseded handover (MM:1721-1729). A review verdict existed only in a message (MM:1731-1739). `CLAUDE.local.md` said `main = origin/main = 9d8c983` while main was `c82e0d2` (JU:74). The always-loaded files were 79,110 B (DR:1510). | UNMEASURED hours; misdirected resumes | State was stored as authored prose in many files | **State is a query:** `hee4 status` prints the tree, dirty count, scoreboard, open asks and newest decisions from the tree and the decision log. The handover is an append-only `decisions.jsonl` plus an `asks` list; there is no free-form restart note. The append target is computed, never remembered. | `hee4 status` output diffed against `git` and the scoreboard (both computed); a planted stale state line in any always-loaded file is flagged by a grep for sha literals. | FACT (counts), INTERP (mechanism) |
| L18 | **Claims relayed without checks.** | The stop-hook verifier flagged relayed agent claims twice (MM:1761-1769). A ruling was made on an author's receipt before the reviews landed, then amended an hour later (MM:936-956). Corrections carried the same overconfidence: 2 of 3 were defective (MM:1431). An instrument was wrong 7 times in one session, always in the dramatic direction (MM:1478-1508). | One amended ruling; UNMEASURED | Receipts are prose; nothing forces a spot-check before a relay | **Typed receipts:** agents return JSON (`claims[]` each with a `witness` command). The relay/synthesis step re-runs a sampled witness per claim and prints `spot_checked=k/n`. A claim with no witness is rendered `UNVERIFIED`. | Plant a receipt with a false witness; synthesis must print it as `CONTRADICTED`. | FACT |
| L19 | **Subagent fan-out cost vs yield.** | 113 defects became 226 refuters; ~9.6 M subagent tokens; the usage limit failed 140 agents and the synthesis (MEM/size-workflows-to-usage-headroom:8-10). 173 agents were killed across 9 runs the tool still reported `completed`; 43 reviewers hit "already used by worktree"; 34 of 55 scripts were lost on tmpfs (MEM/workflow-candidates-note:11-14). Six reviewers were fanned out on an already-answered question (MM:1636-1640). An open-brief reviewer ran 2 h 40 min with no output, where a 20-command brief finished in 6 commands (MEM/recapture-review-needs-a-command-budget:11-14). | ≈9.6 M tokens with no amendments; 2 h 40 min stalled | Fixed per-defect multipliers; no planned-agent budget; open briefs | **Fan-out kernel:** `planned_agents=` is required before the first `agent()`; severity admission (HIGH/MED 2 lenses, LOW ≤ 1); refuters batched `⌈items/5⌉` (FIN:75); every brief has a command budget; `journal.jsonl` spills to durable storage; a pre-fan-out search of same-day handoffs/evidence for the question. | Batching measured 98 planned → 18 agents, 49/49 judged (MEM/size-workflows-to-usage-headroom:22); keep that as a regression fixture. | FACT |
| L20 | **Classifier-refused actions late in a run.** | Lane X was refused 3 times as [Data Exfiltration] after Luke's yes (DR:1869-1871). A push was refused ("Out-of-Place Publication") and Luke's `!` command did not execute over Remote Control (MEM/push-needs-lukes-explicit-command:8-11). A keyring-blocked push hung ~30 min then failed (CM:251). An ownership-transfer message was refused (MM:1755). | ≈30 min hang; lane X never ran | Permission needs are discovered at the moment of action | **Charter-time permission manifest:** the stack charter lists every act needing a human or classifier grant (push, off-machine send, `systemctl enable`, host mutation). A preflight dry-runs each at minute 1 and prints `grant_needed=<act>` for Luke in one message. | Preflight on a charter with `push` and no credentials must print the ask in < 60 s. | FACT |
| L21 | **Ownership confusion between sessions.** | An agent killed another session's mutation run irrecoverably (MM:963-967). A 3,978-mutant job ran in another agent's repo (MM:1255-1263). A peer's "waiting" status was read as a stall and a role transfer attempted (MM:1753-1759). Pattern kills hit my own shell 4 times (#26, #35, #37, #55; MM:1686-1709). Scheduling had to be negotiated ad hoc ("louranicas-88 drives main, every worktree and all cargo", DR:1842). | One irrecoverable run; UNMEASURED | There is no machine-readable lease on shared resources | **Leases:** `~/.local/state/hee4/leases/<resource>.json` (session, pid, since, heartbeat) for `main`, each worktree, the cargo/gate slots and mutation. Cargo wrappers refuse without the lease. Kills go only through a pid file the harness wrote. | Two sessions request the `main` lease: the second must get `held_by=<session>`. A `pkill -f` stays caught by the `pattern-kill` reflex. | FACT |
| L22 | **Commands chained past a failing check.** | A commit was made past `doc rc=101` (MM:591-607). A TOML that did not parse was committed, twice in an hour (MM:988-1014). A plan was truncated and committed in one command (MM:1306-1311). A commit message described an edit that never ran (MM:793-800). | ≈10 min killed gate plus an amend (MM:1325) | Multi-step shell with `set -e` not honoured under `eval` (MM:1010-1011) | **Landing is one tool:** a script ANDs typed check lines and commits only on AND=PASS (NWOW:90, S5). A commit message is generated from `git show --stat`. | The `commit-chain` reflex stays, and the landing tool's control plants a red step and requires no commit. | FACT |
| L23 | **Verdicts taken from pipes.** | Six occurrences (#11, #19, #21, #22, #44, #48; MM:1355-1367, MM:1535-1548). The recurrence share rose from 7/19 to 10/19 (MM:1101). | Recurring | Bash's default (absence = success) aligns with fluency (PR:514-527) | Keep `gate` (it owns the exit code) and emit typed fields, not sentences (PR:552-561). | `pipe-verdict` reflex, proven to fire and to stay quiet. | FACT |
| L24 | **Wrong layer or wrong target.** | A session built context on v2 while the work was v3 (MM:1550-1556). Toolbox `ls` reported a present codebase "missing", and 2,809 host paths read as MISSING (MM:1483, MM:1496-1498). Modules were measured under `src/` alone as stubs three times (`hee-v3-module-homes` memory, per CLAUDE.local). | A whole session (MM:1554) | Paths and targets are ambient conventions | **The repo declares its world:** `hee4.toml` lists module homes and the host/toolbox root. `hee4 status` prints `root=<resolved> view=host|toolbox`. | Run from the toolbox: it must print the `/run/host` root, never an empty dir. | FACT |
| L25 | **Stack branched before a publication or base moved; forced re-gate.** | A stack branched on `89e678c` could not fast-forward past publication `e0c7098`; the cold clone was stopped and the stack re-gated (MEM/publication-commit-sequencing:11-19). | One full gate + cold clone (≈60 min) | Out-of-band commits on `main` (publications) | With no publisher (L9), main advances only by landings. The landing tool rebases and gates once in one chain (S5). | UNMEASURED until v4 lands; count `re-gates` in landing records. | FACT (incident), INTERP (fix) |
| L26 | **Scope-widened rules caused worse quality elsewhere.** (v2) | "Zero new external crates" was applied to dev edges; two crates hand-rolled proptest and tempfile (MM:859-865). A control met the real crate first inside the gate: three runs to green (MM:827-835). | Two degraded test suites; 3 gate runs | A rule's scope was set by gate convenience | Rules declare the **harm they name** and their scope in `rules.toml`; a receipt workaround ("did X because gate refused Y") is a finding logged against the rule. | Grep receipts for the `workaround:` field and require a rule-review row for each. | FACT |
| L27 | **Governance and planning layers grew where nothing counted.** (v2) | Scripts grew +683% against crates +78%; `AUTHORIZATION.md` was the most-edited file (47 touches); 1,246 planning notes were created in one day (PR:606-611). Always-loaded bytes went 79,110 → 77,144 B budget (DR:1510). | UNMEASURED hours | P28: "what is not counted grows" | **Layer denominators printed at every cut:** product, tests, apparatus, governance and planning lines, each with a ratio to product (forge baseline 0.11×, SA:35). | The tag message carries `apparatus_ratio=`, and a cut refuses above a declared bound without a reason line. | FACT |
| L28 | **A roster agent run ends without a typed verdict.** *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F14: first authored as a Loop Register row by the workflow curator; defined here with its source)* | The workflow curator's first light run measured `agent=hee4-workflow-curator runs=5 skipped=0 verdicts: 1 NONE 2 verdict=PASS 2 verdict=PASS_WITH_GAPS` (`~/hee4-evidence/roster/hee4-workflow-curator/measure-20260930T224701Z-light.txt`:5). The NONE run is the selfcheck that wrote `verdict=… — workflow-curator verdict=…` (V4-22). | 1 of 5 runs produced no verdict | the agent's report format was a convention the runner trusted | The runner reads only the report's last non-empty line, matched whole, and exits 30 otherwise (V4-22, V4-26 (a)). | V4-26's stub harness: 32 report shapes, 14 changed exit | FACT |
| L29 | **Same-lineage verification ends PASS_WITH_GAPS every time.** *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F14: first authored as a Loop Register row by the workflow curator; defined here with its source)* | `verification_reports=6`, V1…V6 all `PASS_WITH_GAPS`, 0 PASS (`~/hee4-evidence/roster/hee4-workflow-curator/measure-20260930T224701Z-light.txt`:6-12). V7 and V8 then returned FAIL. Every report is same-lineage; lane X (cross-lineage) is blocked (ATLAS H-6) | UNMEASURED (no cost per report recorded) | a reviewer from the authors' lineage shares their blind spots, so the gap class repeats | INTERP: one cross-lineage pass (H-6) before P0, and a typed verdict per report | a verification report from another lineage; none exists | FACT (counts), INTERP (cause) |
| L30 | **A staged fix verified against the old world, about to be installed into a new one.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | The round-9 boundary passed its own suite 16/16, mutants 9/9, yet refused only the bare token `hee4`: 8 of 17 v4 phrasings (`hee4-contracts`, `hee4db`, `HEE4_RESTART.md`, `HEE v4` …) passed, because markers match on identifier boundaries (DEC V4-74). | an install that would have left P0's JP0 read-back red while every suite read green | the suite's world was v3's; nobody measured the staged door against the v4 namespace it was staged FOR | a world-derived battery (MODULES.toml crates, the hee4 namespace, the homes) run through the real door: `hee4db jev-entry` | `jev_entry_control.py` case `jp0_v4_line_passes`; `tests/v4_family.py` (pre-edit 2/4) | FACT |
| L31 | **A bundle tested file by file, installed as a unit.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | `ctx_test` on the staged files read 6/30 because it paired the staged `jev_cluster` with the INSTALLED boundary (`no attribute 'engine_within'`); with the staged boundary as its documented 4th argument, 30/30 (DEC V4-74). | a correct bundle nearly judged broken; a patched copy of the test written and removed | the test's usage line was read in part; the unit of test ≠ the unit of install | run every suite against the post-install world (the bundle as one library), then again against the installed files | the post-install re-run of every suite on the live paths (V4-74) | FACT |
| L32 | **"Derived by script" with no script.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | The ten ATLAS phase "Blocked by" cells said "derived by script from §5" but were a one-off V11 derivation; after H-8/H-19 closed, the cells still named them while `hee4db recipe blocks-phase P0` printed H-1, H-5, H-27 (DEC V4-74). | a stale P0 hold list in the authority file | a copy labelled as generated, with no generator and no check: a second home (AP-48) | the cell IS the query (`hee4db recipe blocks-phase Pn`); the old list struck | `grep -c 'derived by script from §5 Blocks'` over the ATLAS → 0 | FACT |
| L33 | **A control's first green baseline is its first real test of the design.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | `jev_entry_control.py`, once its own fixture defects were fixed, showed a door that refuses EVERYTHING turned into `verdict=FAIL sent_engine_rows=3/4` (engine rows the broken door invented). Fixed: a wrong control outranks every other answer (UNMEASURED) (DEC V4-74). | a FAIL built on non-evidence, the mirror of a false pass | verdict precedence written before any control exercised it | controls are checked FIRST in the pure policy; a neuter counts only when its case passed on the unneutered code | `jev_entry_control.py` case `clean_control_wrong`, neuter `controls_ignored` | FACT |
| L34 | **"Staged, not installed" in an always-loaded file, while the tree said installed.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | CLAUDE.local listed round-6/round-5 changes as waiting for Luke; `git apply --check` and `git apply -R --check` on the live tree (read-only) showed round-6 steps 1–7 applied, round-5 diffs superseded (DEC V4-74). | an operator would have re-applied or "fixed" live code from a stale list | state written as text (AP-46) | measure applied state both ways before acting; state lines become dated corrections pointing at the read-back | the read-only forward/reverse check, recorded per step in V4-74 | FACT |
| L35 | **A mutant that does not run is scored as a survivor or a kill.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | `v4_family.py`'s first mutant run: a deletion that broke the `V4_FAMILY` tuple crashed the child and printed SURVIVED; `jev_entry_control.py`'s first run counted 11/11 neuter kills on a red baseline (DEC V4-74). | a false survivor (wasted rule work) and false kills (a control certifying nothing) | the harness read "no case went red/green" without asking whether the mutated code ran | INVALID is a third outcome; mutate by making a pattern unmatchable, not by deleting syntax; neuters require a green baseline case | both harnesses print `INVALID` and refuse to count it | FACT |
| L36 | **An edit to a patched file silently breaks the patch's undo.** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74)* | The F-B scan edited `jev-verify-claim` inside the context of round-6 step 3's diff; `git apply -R --check` then failed at `:297`, so APPLY-ORDER's undo line no longer worked (DEC V4-74). | an undo that fails at the moment it is needed | undo kept as a reverse diff against a file other changes may touch | every install writes its own exact `restore.sh` of whole files; the undo order is written where the undo lives (APPLY-ORDER 2026-10-02 note) | `git apply -R --check` re-run after any later edit to a patched file | FACT |

**Row count:** *(rev 2026-10-02 V4-74: **36**, L30–L36 appended from the Jev fix session)* 27 loops *(rev 2026-10-01 V7/V8/V9/V10-fix, V7 F14)*: **29** since L28 and L29 were appended from the roster's first light run; the 27 counts below describe L1–L27. Every row cites a FACT incident. L1, L2, L17 and L25 also carry an INTERP cost or mechanism. L14, L17, L18, L21, L25 and L27 have costs UNMEASURED in whole or in part.

## 2 · Rules that worked: keep in v4

| # | Rule | Evidence | Tag |
|---|---|---|---|
| K1 | **Independent review of every slice on committed objects** | "Nearly every real defect came from independent review, planted faults and mutation" (SA:59). The peer reviewer's every HIGH was real (`~/handoffs/HEE3_HANDOVER_20260930_1400.md:38-40`). A second lineage found 6 defects in one session, 0 disputed (MM:1397-1399, MM:1431-1435). | FACT |
| K2 | **Plant batteries with named killers under `--cap-lints=warn`** | 842/868 killed, every survivor a real gap (NWOW:19). `verdict=PASS plants=78 killed=78 … not_compiled=0 hung=0` (`B14-store-runtime-20260926/DESIGN.md:4375`). | FACT |
| K3 | **Scoped mutation on store and policy code, runner-owned target dir** | RA2 found ≈17 real gaps in 178 mutants (DR:1809-1811). The workspace sweep found 21 in landed code (MM:1334-1336). | FACT |
| K4 | **The flow ratchet (`l2=` before and after) with a host-record L2 kind** | `l2` 2 → 3 at `dfb32d5`, the first move in 46+ landings, about 2 days after adoption (LR-dfb32d5:13). Every landing record since carries the brake line (LR-7ed3728:28, LR-0c3757a:24). | FACT |
| K5 | **At most 2 design rounds, then land the buildable cut; skeleton before review** | B14c-E closed as a disposition instead of a third round (DR:1484-1491). The forge had no design rounds (SA:33). | FACT (the rule was applied); the benefit is INTERP |
| K6 | **The detector budget (the brake)** | B14c-E was stopped and replaced by a one-line re-measure (DR:1491). Re-measure trigger recorded. | FACT |
| K7 | **`gate` and reflexes: the right form made shorter, and the rule moved to the claim** | PR:535-543. The corpus-measure and host-path hooks fired in production the turn they were installed (MM:1523-1526). Their proofs: `cases=11/11`, `cases=14/14` (MM:1515-1519). | FACT |
| K8 | **`hee3-gate` flock slots and the gated-worktree guard** | These removed the voided-gate and 3-gate contention class (NWOW:88). | FACT (built); effect UNMEASURED |
| K9 | **Batching refuters by severity; UNJUDGED ≠ REFUTED** | 98 planned refuters → 18 agents, 49/49 judged, 0 missing (MEM/size-workflows-to-usage-headroom:22-23). | FACT |
| K10 | **Command-budgeted briefs; file-as-evidence, a ≤ 15-line pointer return** | 6 commands and under a minute, against 2 h 40 min open-ended (MEM/recapture-review-needs-a-command-budget:11-14). FIN:49-50. | FACT |
| K11 | **Landing record written before the fast-forward, typed lines ANDed as one unit** | Every T28 landing since 09-29 (LR-0c3757a:3-19, LR-0b4637e:8-16). The one out-of-order case was recorded as such (LR-7ed3728:6). | FACT |
| K12 | **"State is a query, never a field"; intent keeps an independent origin** | All 18 stale or wrong status rows were authored state (JU:107). The scoreboard (derived) tracked the code (JU:28, JU:58). | FACT |
| K13 | **Enumerate before any blanket act** | The reclaim near-miss: `sorted()` would have deleted every graphify run (DR:1631). `done=293 failed=0` (DR:1629). | FACT |
| K14 | **Push discipline: explicit word, secret scan with its control, `ls-remote` read-back** | Every push since 09-29 read back `ls-remote` equal to local, with `hits=0` (DR:1849, DR:1866, DR:1874). | FACT |
| K15 | **`include_census`: a gate input derived, not listed** | It converted a thrice-recurring 25-minute failure into a named refusal (MEM/hee3-gate-declared-inputs:24-28). | FACT (built); recurrence since UNMEASURED |
| K16 | **Compiler/symbol-decided checks over source censuses** | The raw-v0 symbol re-measure replaced the census and its 5 false passes (DR:1478-1491, RA5 DR:1538). | FACT |

## 3 · Top 10 structural scaffolding requirements for v4, ranked by measured cost

| Rank | Requirement | Loops closed | Measured cost it addresses |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **A derived, tiered, diff-scoped gate with one runner.** No count literals. Tiers declared in `gate.toml` (commit / stack / cut). The precount is generated from the gate. Dev, precount and gate share the subreaper runner. | L1, L2, L3, L5, L6 | 38.6 machine-h / 105 runs, 18% measuring nothing; ≈80 min per landing; 75% of src commits churn count literals (SA:48, SA:57, NWOW:17) |
| 2 | **No publisher and no generated blocks in source.** Intent rows in the repo with a named reader; state computed on read; the version cut is a tag carrying `flows= l2= evidenced=`. | L9, L10, L11, L25 | 18–44 min per publication; 4/20 and 4/10 failed; ≈2 h of metadata failures; 296 GB reclaimed; 30 files with false text (DR:1580, NWOW:20, DR:1629, JU:45) |
| 3 | **A fan-out kernel.** `planned_agents=` before launch, severity admission, batched refuters, command-budgeted briefs, durable journal spill, a pre-fan-out search for same-day answers, typed receipts with witness commands. | L18, L19 | ≈9.6 M tokens with 140 agents failed; 173 killed while "completed"; 2 h 40 min stalled reviewer (MEM/size-workflows…:8-10, MEM/workflow-candidates-note:11-14) |
| 4 | **A skeleton-first slice state machine.** `slice new` gives a one-page FLOW and a compiling skeleton; the review tool refuses an uncompiled subject and a round 3; a detector admission header (trigger, budget, reader). | L12, L13 | R23 alone 659,219 tokens; B14 4,412 design lines; B14c-E 2,319 lines ≈5.4 h (CA:85-91, SA:61) |
| 5 | **Hermetic provisioning.** `provision` materialises every fetched input (offline crate bundle, SQLite amalgamation) from a content-addressed manifest; the gate's step 0 refuses a missing input by name in seconds. | L4 | ≈25 min × 3 undeclared-input failures; 13 tests erroring in every fresh worktree (MEM/hee3-gate-declared-inputs:11-22, WAVE1-INTEGRATION.md:67-69) |
| 6 | **Snapshot-subject gates plus load admission.** The gate runs on its own `--detach` / `git archive` at a sha, never the live worktree. Slots are flocked. Each step prints `elapsed/budget`, and tests use logical clocks. | L7, L8 | 11/64 runs measured nothing; ≈25 min × voided gates; 50 min per load-induced timeout; t21 12 s margin (NWOW:22, MEM/no-builds-beside-a-gate:11-19) |
| 7 | **One battery and mutation harness.** Killers resolved against `--list`; `--cap-lints=warn`; fresh-mtime restore plus `cargo clean -p`; pid file; frozen index; NOT_COMPILED/HUNG count as survivors; the mutation runner owns its target dir with a precheck plant; "owed" is not a landing state. | L14, L15 | A whole mutation run void (21/57 hand-plant fails); 21 survivors landed; `store-doors` 0 tested twice (MEM/mutation-target-dir-trap:14-15, MM:1334, FIN:25) |
| 8 | **Leases and a charter-time permission manifest.** Machine-readable leases for main, worktrees, cargo slots and mutation. Every grant-needing act (push, off-machine send, unit enable) is enumerated and preflighted at minute 1. | L20, L21 | An irrecoverable killed run; a ~30 min push hang; lane X never ran after Luke's yes (MM:963-967, CM:251, DR:1869-1871) |
| 9 | **One door per rule.** `rules.toml` maps rule → exactly one enforcing site, with the harm named and the scope stated. A parsed census refuses duplicate sites, and receipt workarounds are logged against the rule. | L16, L26 | 9 refusals from a scratch gate; 2 h with three documents wrong; 2 degraded suites (MM:1600-1610, MM:803-805, MM:859-865) |
| 10 | **State as a query plus an append-only decision log.** `hee4 status` computes tree, dirty count, scoreboard and asks; the handover is `decisions.jsonl` plus asks; the append target is computed; layer denominators (`apparatus_ratio=`) are printed at every cut. | L17, L22, L24, L27 | 21 handoff files, 714,986 B *(measured now)*; a whole session on the wrong codebase; stale state in always-loaded files (MM:1554, JU:74). Hours are UNMEASURED, so this ranks last. |

**Ranking basis.** Ranks 1–2 are machine-hours and hours of wall time printed in the sources. Rank 3 is tokens and agents. Ranks 4–7 are per-incident minutes multiplied by recorded recurrences. Ranks 8–10 carry real incidents whose time cost is mostly UNMEASURED; they rank below the measured costs, not below the risks they carry. The discovery layer (K1–K3) is a floor, not a ranked item: RA6 exempts it from the brake (DR:1540).

## 4 · Not measured

- The time cost per incident for L14, L17, L18, L21 and L27.
- Whether the tiered gate (rank 1) would have caught the same zero product defects. The gate's history says confirmation found ≈0 (NWOW:18, SA:57), but that is a window, not a law.
- Guard precision for warn-only reflexes (AH:215: "guard precision is UNMEASURED").
- The Zellij-side session receipts (SA:25).
